<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs mixed in New York, Dow up 30 points.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs mixed in New York, Dow up 30 points.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>NZ ADRs were mixed in late New York trade, where by 7.30 a.m. NZT the Dow was up 29.67 points at 7,224.34.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.     17/09	     -0/01  *</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$27 1/2	 -0 1/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$32 1/8	  nil   *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$21 7/8	 -0 3/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$13 1/8	 +0 1/8 *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$36 3/4	  nil   *</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  41 1/2	     +2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  235 1/2	   -0 1/2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  159 1/2	   -2 1/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  151 1/2	    +1</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.20	     nil</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.72	     nil</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$2.18	     nil</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of eight shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
